<title>USA: Top 10 movies at U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are movie ticket sales at the U.S. box office for the July 25-27 weekend, according to studio estimates from Exhibitor Relations Co. Final data will be issued on Monday.</p>
<p> 1 (*) Air Force One ..........................  $37.1 million</p>
<p> 2 (2) George of the Jungle .................... $13.2 million</p>
<p> 3 (1) Men in Black ............................ $12.6 million</p>
<p> 4 (3) Contact .................................  $9.5 million</p>
<p> 5 (*) Good Burger .............................  $7.3 million</p>
<p> 6 (4) Nothing To Lose .........................  $6.7 million</p>
<p> 7 (5) Face/Off ................................  $5.6 million</p>
<p> 8 (6) My Best Friend's Wedding ................  $4.5 million</p>
<p> 9 (7) Hercules ................................  $2.9 million</p>
<p> 10(8) Operation Condor ........................  $1.6 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Last weekend's position in parentheses. * denotes new release.</p>
<p>&quot;Air Force One&quot; and &quot;Men in Black&quot; are released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp. Sony's TriStar studio released &quot;My Best Friend's Wedding.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;George of the Jungle,&quot; &quot;Nothing to Lose&quot; and &quot;Hercules&quot; are from Walt Disney Co.</p>
<p>Disney's Miramax Films unit released &quot;Operation Condor.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Contact&quot; is released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Good Burger&quot; and &quot;Face/Off&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.</p>
